       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled prescription dose of ibuprofen. The usual limits are:\n\n- **Single dose:** 800 mg at most.\n- **Daily total:** 3,200 mg at most. Many clinicians use 2,400 mg/day or less.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It wouldn't be expected to give more pain or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (typical for pain or inflammation)\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided** (for example, 400 mg four times daily)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
